preConditionHook:
// PERMISSION TO TAKE A COUNTERTREND TRADE: the side you are about to join must
// have shown it can move price at all. At least one of the lookback bars BEFORE
// this one pushed its high more than minPushTicks above the high of the bar
// before it (mirrored on lows for a countertrend short). T10-07's cheap version
// of "there must have been a prior break of the trend line" -- no pivots, no
// line, which is why it is worth testing as the poor man's substitute for
// CountertrendNeedsPriorTrendLineBreak.
//
// AN EXISTENCE TEST OVER BARS 1..lookback, not a count and not the current bar:
// the permission is evidence that ALREADY EXISTS when this bar's signal appears.
// Written as an explicit loop in both twins rather than EL CountIF, which counts
// bars 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar -- the wrong window here.
//
// STRICT: the source says "more than", so a push of exactly minPushTicks does
// not qualify; el_gt carries the measured 2.22e-12 relational tolerance.
// Not LaggedHigherHigh, which asks whether ONE specific bar made a higher high,
// with no margin and no window.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables entry,
// never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
// Deepest bar touched: lookback + 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
pushedUp = false;
pushedDn = false;
for (int i = 1; i <= (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i] - high[i + 1], minPushTicks * tickSize)) pushedUp = true;
    if (el_gt(low[i + 1] - low[i], minPushTicks * tickSize)) pushedDn = true;
}
